    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:4b5ff9b4a37f43cc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "4bab7fec4ec141dc9fb6b25ce92b0f4737002d81cd13143f3ba62791f0fbb489",
      "text": "Day 3 · After a typical Brazilian breakfast, your driver takes you to the foot of Corcovado through the leafy neighbourhoods of Botafogo and Laranjeiras. A small train, the same line that once carried the materials for the statue to the summit, winds through the rainforest, where you may spot monkeys jumping from tree to tree, as the city becomes smaller below. At the foot of the 30-metre statue of Christ the Redeemer, a stunning panorama reveals all of Rio, from Leblon, Ipanema and the Lagoon to the centre, Maracanã Stadium, the Sambadrome and far into Guanabara Bay.\n\nAfterwards, a tour around the Rodrigo de Freitas Lagoon, a perfect family spot to ride along the waterfront on a bike or even a swan boat. Kids will love the many birds, and sometimes families of capybaras, the world’s largest rodents.",
