    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:ec46e3209ab74818",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "0ce2a242db2de23a15fc9226ef53e4acd6667ea096ef3be49bee72729ab72e14",
      "text": "Day 4 · A free day, or choose one of the recommended optional tours (see Optional excursions).\n\nOptional excursions   at an additional cost\n\nRecommended optional tours for your free day in Rio, bookable on request.\n\nBotanical Garden\n\nRio · Day 4 · 4 hours\n\nPrice on request\n\nA magnificent 137-hectare garden more than 200 years old, with thousands of plant species, orchids, bromeliads, cacti and giant bamboo in the shadow of Corcovado; capybaras are sometimes seen near the pond of giant water lilies.\n\nTropical islands\n\nRio · Day 4 · 8 hours\n\nPrice on request\n\nFrom the fishing village of Itacuruçá, a boat trip among tropical islands, with a chance to see dolphins and sea turtles, time to swim in crystal-clear water and lunch on an island.\n\nSamba show\n\nRio · evening · 4 hours\n\nPrice on request\n\nDinner included\n\nAn unforgettable night of Brazilian music and dance, with samba and capoeira performers, dinner during the show and return to your hotel.\n\nRocinha community tour\n\nRio · private · 4 hours\n\nPrice on request\n\nDiscover Rocinha, one of Rio’s largest and best-known communities, with a local guide: its streets, history, culture and everyday life.\n\nHelicopter flight over Rio\n\nFrom Sugar Loaf or Lagoa · 8–9 minutes\n\nPrice on request\n\nChrist the Redeemer, Sugar Loaf, the Two Brothers mountain and the curves of Copacabana and Ipanema from the sky.",
